<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41041" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕ-miscĕo</span></b> , no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>, mixtum or
				mistum, 2, v. a., <i>to
				mix</i> or <i>mingle again</i>, <i>to mix up</i>, <i>intermingle</i> (perh. only in
			the foll. passages). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">venenum remixtum cibo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Const. 7, 4</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sic veris falsa remiscet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. A.
					P. 151</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animus naturae suae remiscebitur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 71, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">remixto carmine tibiis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 4, 15, 30</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>